    description: "MEASURED 2026-09-17 at 06699b1d91. HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 hypergumbo survey\n~/whole_bunch_of_repos/aardvark-dns (16 .rs, Rust-only). Backend confirmed\nactive on stderr. This is the ROOT CAUSE row for WI-jivim's violation count and\nWI-zabus's missing symbol join; both are the same defect seen from two sides.\n\nTHE BACKEND WORKS. It is the largest producer in the artifact:\n\n    nodes origin=['scip']   669  of 1255   (53%)\n    edges origin=['scip']   637  of 1550   (41%)   -- vs tree-sitter rust's 445\n\nALL OF IT IS ORPHANED:\n\n    669 scip nodes  ->  origin_run_id == ''            (669 Symbol violations)\n    637 scip edges  ->  one fabricated UUID            (637 Edge violations)\n    1308 cross_field validation violations total (669 + 637 + 2 unrelated)\n    rust_analyzer appears in NEITHER analysis_runs NOR limits.skipped_passes\n      (74 + 84 = 158 passes; it is in none) -- and it is the ONLY one of 118\n      registered analyzers for which that is true.\n\nTHE CHAIN, three links, each individually reasonable:\n\n1. analyzer.py:215 success path returns\n       return AnalysisResult(symbols=symbols, edges=edges)\n   with no run=, so AnalysisResult.run defaults to None.\n\n2. collect_analyzer_result's run-is-None branch records a skip ONLY when\n   produced_nothing is true. This producer emitted 1306 records, so it is\n   drained and then dropped from the accounting. The branch comment names this\n   exactly -- \"a producer that emitted symbols/edges without a run is a\n   distinct anomaly (e.g. rust_analyzer's success path returns run=None with\n   SCIP output) -- keep its output, don't mislabel it a skip\" -- and\n   deliberately records nothing. Keeping the output is right; recording\n   nothing is what breaks WI-didil.\n\n3. translate.py:189-198 FABRICATES A RUN PURELY TO SATISFY A GUARD:\n\n       # WI-higap: if no run_id is supplied (legacy callers), create a local\n       # run so Edge.__post_init__ enforcement passes.\n       if not run_id:\n           _scip_run = AnalysisRun.create(pass_id=make_pass_id(\"rust-scip-translate\"), ...)\n           run_id = _scip_run.execution_id\n\n   The AnalysisRun object is constructed, its execution_id harvested, and the\n   object discarded. Nothing ever serializes it.\n\nTHE ESCAPE HATCH EXISTS AND IS UNREACHABLE. translate_scip_to_hg takes\nrun_id=\"\" and its comment says \"Callers that want provenance to flow into a\nparent run can pass run_id explicitly.\" No production caller can:\ngraceful_degrade.py:192 calls translate_fn(scip_bytes, source_reader) with no\nrun_id, and try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer has no run_id parameter to forward.\nSo every production call takes the fabricating branch. The parameter is\nreachable only from tests.\n\nTHE GUARD MADE IT WORSE, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF THIS ROW. Edge.__post_init__\nhard-raises on empty origin_run_id (WI-higap) to prevent silent provenance\nloss. Symbol has no such guard. Observe the consequence:\n\n    Symbols (unguarded) -> origin_run_id ''          honest, visibly empty\n    Edges   (guarded)   -> 'uuid:40421dc5-...'       well-formed, resolves to nothing\n\nWithout the guard the edges would be empty like the symbols -- one obvious\ndefect. With it they carry a syntactically valid UUID that passes every\nstructural check and fails only the FK join. The guard converted an honest\nabstention into a confident wrong answer. That is the ABSENT != EMPTY defect\ninverted: a manufactured value satisfying an invariant designed to prove the\nvalue was not manufactured.\n\nTHE FIX IS THE SAME ONE FOR ALL THREE SYMPTOMS. Build a real AnalysisRun in\nanalyzer.py's success path, thread its execution_id through\ntry_analyze_with_rust_analyzer into translate_scip_to_hg's existing run_id\nparameter, and return it as AnalysisResult(run=...). That single change:\n  - gives the pass an analysis_runs entry (restores WI-didil completeness)\n  - resolves all 637 dangling edge FKs\n  - gives the 669 symbols a run to join to (closes WI-zabus)\n  - lets the fabricating branch in translate.py be deleted, or narrowed to\n    genuinely test-only callers\nNo schema change. No owner decision -- this is a bug, not an accounting policy\nquestion.\n\nWHY IT WAS NOT CAUGHT. The backend is opt-in and off by default, so no CI run\nand no bakeoff exercises the success path; the validator reports the violations\nas a [warn] line, not a failure. WI-jivim's Aug-23 measurement used a\n3-function fixture and saw 16 violations, which read as a rounding error rather\nthan \"every scip record in the artifact\".\n\nRELATED: WI-jivim (P2, the bundle this explains), WI-zabus (P3, the symbol\nhalf), WI-luvud (P3, the failure path -- a different branch of the same\nfunction), WI-mamiv (P2, the AR-or-skip host boundary this adds a third\noutcome to)."  # aa23
    fields: {}  # aa23
