  clock: 3  # b604
  nonce: b604  # b604
  message: "FIXED in f685e584ef. Closed on a re-run of this row's OWN filed repro, not a\nproxy.\n\nREPRO, verbatim from the description:\n    HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 hypergumbo survey ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/aardvark-dns\n\n                                        BEFORE          AFTER\n    rust_analyzer in analysis_runs      no              YES\n    rust_analyzer in skipped_passes     no              no\n    passes accounted (runs + skips)     74 + 84 = 158   75 + 84 = 159\n    scip nodes / dangling               669 / 669       669 / 0\n    scip edges / dangling               637 / 637       637 / 0\n    cross_field validation violations   1308            2\n\nThe 2 survivors are unrelated and pre-existing: one degenerate\nSymbol.fingerprint and one stable_id collision. Every origin_run_id violation\nis gone.\n\nTHE FIX, three links matching the three in the description:\n\n1. analyzer.py mints the AnalysisRun BEFORE dispatch and returns it:\n   AnalysisResult(run=run, symbols=..., edges=...).\n2. try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer gains a run_id parameter and forwards it to\n   the translator -- the missing link that made translate_scip_to_hg's\n   documented escape hatch reachable from production for the first time.\n   TranslateFn is promoted from a Callable alias to a Protocol, because\n   Callable cannot express a keyword-only argument and widening it to\n   Callable[..., ...] would drop checking on the seam every graceful-degrade\n   test injects through.\n3. translate_scip_to_hg now stamps SYMBOLS with the same run_id it already\n   stamped on edges. That closes WI-zabus at the source rather than relying on\n   the orchestrator's WI-mosil backstop, which only fills EMPTY ids and which a\n   library caller bypassing the orchestrator never reaches.\n\nPlus the orchestrator backstop: collect_analyzer_result now synthesizes an\nAnalysisRun for a productive run-less producer instead of dropping it, with a\nwarning naming it a producer defect. Recording a skip there would be a lie --\nthe output proves the pass ran. That run IS serialized, so unlike the\nfabrication this row was filed about, the FK it carries resolves.\n\nTHE FABRICATING BRANCH IS DELIBERATELY KEPT. translate_scip_to_hg still\nfalls back to a local run when a caller supplies none, because the function is\nexported and a direct library caller with no parent run should not be forced to\ninvent one. What changed is that it now stamps both halves from that id, so a\ndangling artifact is ONE fact a reader can chase instead of two\nunrelated-looking ones -- and no production path reaches it any more.\n\nTESTS: 6 written RED first, all now green. The end-to-end one\n(TestProvenanceJoin::test_every_emitted_record_joins_to_the_returned_run) runs\nthe REAL degrade + translate chain against a real SCIP blob and asserts zero\ndangling FKs, so it fails if any of the three links regresses. Full suite 4835\npassed, mypy ratchet 667 (delta +0).\n\nNOT CLAIMED: the duplicate method-kind symbols and the raw-vs-deduplicated edge\ncount (edges_emitted 1272 vs 637 surviving) are untouched and remain on\nWI-jivim."  # b604
